# Copy this file to .env and fill in values for your setup. .env itself is
# gitignored - only this .example file is meant to be committed.

# Where the frontend sends API requests. Leave this UNSET (or delete the
# line) for the normal setup: frontend and backend served from the same
# origin, with Vite's dev proxy (see vite.config.ts) or your production
# reverse proxy forwarding /api to the backend - requests then just use a
# relative /api/... path, exactly as this app worked before this file
# existed.
#
# Only set this when the frontend is deployed on a DIFFERENT origin/domain
# than the backend (the scenario the backend's own CROSS_SITE_FRONTEND
# setting exists for - see backend/.env) - e.g. the frontend is on Vercel
# and the backend is on your own VPS under a different domain. Point it at
# the backend's own origin, no trailing slash and no /api suffix:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.madgen.space
